## General Workflow Principles

### Before Starting Any Change
1. Read relevant existing code
2. Search for similar implementations
3. Understand the current architecture
4. Identify integration points (EventBus, EntityFactory, GameState, etc.)

### During Implementation
1. Make small, incremental changes
2. Test frequently (after every 10-15 minutes)
3. Keep console output clean (no errors/warnings)
4. Use guard clauses and null checks liberally

### After Completion
1. Run full playtest (at least one complete stage)
2. Check performance (should maintain 60 FPS)
3. Review console output for errors/warnings
4. Update related documentation/configs
5. Commit with clear, descriptive message

### If Stuck
1. Search codebase for similar patterns (`grep`, `Ctrl+Shift+F`)
2. Check `.cursor/rules/` for guidance
3. Read related manager/system code
4. Add debug logging to understand behavior
5. Simplify the problem (minimal reproduction)
6. Ask for clarification if truly blocked

**These workflows ensure consistent, safe, and repeatable development.**
